WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.940
Every sale starts as someone seeing you.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.660
Most of them never get to the end.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:06.920
Where do they go?

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.340
This is the funnel, and what a sale costs.

5
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.300
The funnel is made up of the actions

6
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.260
your potential customers have to take.

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.760
The first stage is the impression,
when the ad, the result, or the post is seen.

8
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.150
That is one hundred percent.

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.960
The second stage is engagement, a click,
which is the first action they take.

10
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.540
That is eight percent.

11
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.100
The third stage is the action,
a form, a call, or a step into the site.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.710
That is two percent.

13
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.580
The last stage is goal fulfilled,
the conversion that pays for it all.

14
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.380
That is zero point six percent.

15
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.820
These rates are illustrative,

16
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.140
but the shape is not.

17
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.600
Every extra step you add loses people,

18
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.920
so a step has to earn its place.

19
00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.080
Now work it backwards.

20
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.300
You need six sales.

21
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.400
How many impressions

22
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.880
does the top of the funnel need?

23
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.630
Six sales, at zero point six percent,

24
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.400
is a thousand impressions.

25
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.180
And that is how a media budget gets sized.

26
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.380
All traffic sources bring value,

27
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:11.640
every one of them.

28
00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.240
But every traffic source also has a cost,

29
00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.020
including the ones that look free.

30
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.660
Content costs time,

31
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.140
and time costs money.

32
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.300
Operate by a clear economic model,

33
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.940
or you cannot tell a good channel from a bad one.

34
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.090
If a lead costs thirty dollars,

35
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.660
and one in five leads becomes a sale,

36
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.400
a sale costs a hundred and fifty dollars in marketing.

37
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.040
If the customer is worth four hundred dollars,

38
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.120
the channel works.

39
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.720
If they are worth a hundred and twenty,

40
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:39.420
it does not,

41
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.240
no matter how good the creative is.

42
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.720
Understand this one calculation,

43
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.820
and you can hold a conversation with a finance director.

44
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.900
Next, work the funnel backwards

45
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.100
with your own numbers.

